+// coop-snapshot (port/src/coop/snapshot_state.cpp): the VM's host-side state, each
+// interpreter's stacks and the decoded function records, lived on the C heap, where two copies of the game hold it at
+// different addresses; a snapshot taken on one copy then put the other's script objects onto memory that was not there
+// (the monsters' scripts run every floor tick). It now comes from one arena block of its own, pinned with the rest under
+// DC_FIXED_LAYOUT, so both copies hold it at one address and it goes with the arenas into every snapshot. Nothing is
+// ever given back: a stack grows at most a few times, a record is decoded once per place in a loaded file.
+constexpr std::size_t kVmArenaBytes = 48u << 20;
+int                   g_vm_arena_owner; // the block's owner (its address picks the pinned slot)
+
